  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe model breakdown misclassifies Codex CLI sessions that use the OpenCode Go plugin and assigns an unsupported price to DeepSeek V4 Flash.\n\n## Current behavior\n\n- Codex stores the plugin model as `model_provider=openai` with model ID `opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash`.\n- The dashboard displays it as an OpenAI model instead of OpenCode Go.\n- Non-free `deepseek-v4-flash` receives a price from the hardcoded/OpenRouter pricing path even though no trusted provider rate is configured.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n- Decode `opencode-go/<model>` and `opencode-free/<model>` namespaces from Codex model IDs.\n- Display the provider as OpenCode Go/OpenCode Free rather than OpenAI.\n- Keep non-free DeepSeek V4 Flash unpriced until a trusted rate is available.\n- Keep the explicit `deepseek-v4-flash-free` variant at zero cost.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Add regression coverage for Codex provider normalization.\n- Add regression coverage for paid DeepSeek V4 Flash remaining unpriced even when remote pricing is present.\n- Add regression coverage for the explicit free variant.\n",
